The sample points defined in the two figures are: 

 (\mathbf{A})
\begin{array}{lll}{P}_{11}=\left(0,\frac{1}{2}\right)\amp {P}_{21}=\left(\frac{1}{2},\frac{1}{4}\right)\amp {P}_{31}=( 1,0 )\\ \noalign{\smallskip}
{P}_{12}=\left(\frac{1}{3},\frac{3}{4}\right)\amp {P}_{22}=\left(\frac{1}{2},1\right)\amp {P}_{32}=\left(\frac{5}{6},\frac{3}{4}\right)\end{array}
(\mathbf{B})
\begin{array}{lll}{P}_{11}=\left(\frac{1}{2},\frac{1}{3}\right)\amp {P}_{21}=\left(\frac{3}{4},\frac{1}{6}\right)\amp {P}_{12}=\left(0,\frac{1}{2}\right)\\ \noalign{\smallskip}
{P}_{22}=\left(1,\frac{2}{3}\right)\amp {P}_{13}=\left(\frac{1}{4},\frac{5}{6}\right)\amp {P}_{23}=\left(\frac{3}{4},\frac{5}{6}\right)\end{array}
We compute the values of f( x,y )=2(x+y) at the sample points:


(\mathbf{A})
f\left({P}_{11}\right)=f\left(0,\frac{1}{2}\right)=2\left(0+\frac{1}{2}\right)=2\cdot\frac{1}{2} f\left({P}_{21}\right)=f\left(\frac{1}{2},\frac{1}{4}\right)=2\left(\frac{1}{2}+\frac{1}{4}\right)=2\cdot\frac{3}{4} f\left({P}_{31}\right)=f( 1,0 )=2(1+0)=2
f\left({P}_{12}\right)=f\left(\frac{1}{3},\frac{3}{4}\right)=2\left(\frac{1}{3}+\frac{3}{4}\right)=2\cdot\frac{13}{12} f\left({P}_{22}\right)=f\left(\frac{1}{2},1\right)=2\left(\frac{1}{2}+1\right)=2\cdot\frac{3}{2}
f\left({P}_{32}\right)=f\left(\frac{5}{6},\frac{3}{4}\right)=2\left(\frac{5}{6}+\frac{3}{4}\right)=2\cdot\frac{19}{12}
Each subrectangle has sides of length \Delta x=\frac{1}{3}, \Delta y=\frac{1}{2} and area \Delta A=\Delta x\Delta y=\frac{1}{3}\cdot \frac{1}{2}=\frac{1}{6}. 

 We obtain the following Riemann sum:
{S}_{32} =
\sum_{i=1}^3\sum_{j=1}^2f\left({P}_{ij}\right)\Delta A=\frac{2}{6}\left(\frac{1}{2}+\frac{3}{4}+1+\frac{13}{12}+\frac{3}{2}+\frac{19}{12}\right)=
\frac{2\cdot 77}{72}\approx 2.13889

(\mathbf{B})

f\left({P}_{11}\right)=f\left(\frac{1}{2},\frac{1}{3}\right)=2\left(\frac{1}{2}+\frac{1}{3}\right)=2\cdot\frac{5}{6} f\left({P}_{21}\right)=f\left(\frac{3}{4},\frac{1}{6}\right)=2\left(\frac{3}{4}+\frac{1}{6}\right)=2\cdot\frac{11}{12} f\left({P}_{12}\right)=f\left(0,\frac{1}{2}\right)=2\left(0+\frac{1}{2}\right)=2\cdot\frac{1}{2} f\left({P}_{22}\right)=f\left(1,\frac{2}{3}\right)=2\left(1+\frac{2}{3}\right)=2\cdot\frac{5}{3} f\left({P}_{13}\right)=f\left(\frac{1}{4},\frac{5}{6}\right)=2\left(\frac{1}{4}+\frac{5}{6}\right)=2\cdot\frac{13}{12} f\left({P}_{23}\right)=f\left(\frac{3}{4},\frac{5}{6}\right)=2\left(\frac{3}{4}+\frac{5}{6}\right)=2\cdot\frac{19}{12}
Each subrectangle has sides of length \Delta x=\frac{1}{2}, \Delta y=\frac{1}{3} 


and area \Delta A=\Delta x\Delta y=\frac{1}{2}\cdot \frac{1}{3}=\frac{1}{6}. 


We obtain the following Riemann sum:
{S}_{23} =\sum_{i=1}^3\sum_{j=1}^2f\left({P}_{ij}\right)\Delta A=\frac{2}{6}\left(\frac{5}{6}+\frac{11}{12}+\frac{1}{2}+\frac{5}{3}+\frac{13}{12}+
\frac{19}{12}\right)
=\frac{2\cdot 79}{72}\approx 2.19444
